    "problem_statement": "Add a new memory-pool API os_mempool_clear(struct os_mempool *mp) that invalidates/reinitializes all blocks of an already-initialized mempool back to a fully-free state without a full re-initialization, and that can be called multiple times on the same mempool (unlike init). It must return OS_INVALID_PARM for a NULL pool and OS_OK otherwise, resetting mp_num_free/mp_min_free and re-chaining all blocks into the free list. The os_mempool unit test must be able to call this function to clear the pool mid-test and re-run the full allocate/free/assert sequence, verifying the pool returns to a consistent fully-free state.",
